<article class="env-lemma" id="3BA6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/3BA6">Lemma <span data-tag="3BA6">5.3.3.2</span>.</a> Let $F \in \Fun (K,\SSet )$ be a <em>corepresentable</em> functor (that is, $F$ lies in the essential image of the Yoneda embedding $K^{op} \rightarrow \Fun (K,\SSet )$), and let $X \in \SSet $ be a colimit of $F$. Then $X$ is contractible. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Without loss of generality, we may suppose that $K$ is an $\infty $-category. Let $\widetilde{K} \rightarrow K$ be a left fibration classified by $F$. Since $F$ is corepresentable, $\widetilde{K}$ has an initial object and is therefore weakly contractible. Corollary <a href="/tag/ABDF" data-tag="ABDF">3.3.4.6</a> implies that there is an isomorphism $\widetilde{K} \simeq X$ in the homotopy category $\calH $, so that $X$ is also contractible. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>